{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:02IR:title", "parent_tag": "02IR", "chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "section_title", "risk_level": "R1", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Regular schemes", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-regular}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:f8aeccbd4184a2f6d85f196a01c7bb384d346aed10b52541dede044065b1b7aa", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:439aba7bb6ca34f44674bdd794e13f1819d63c2ac6069a1e07242bc6f09a884e", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:02IR:prose-0001", "parent_tag": "02IR", "chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "risk_level": "R2", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nRecall, see Algebra, Definition <REF_0001>,\nthat a local Noetherian ring <MATH_0001> is\nsaid to be <TEXTITOPEN_0001>regular<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if <MATH_0002> can be generated\nby <MATH_0003> elements.\nRecall that a Noetherian ring <MATH_0004> is said to be <TEXTITOPEN_0002>regular<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> if\nevery local ring <MATH_0005> of <MATH_0006> is regular,\nsee Algebra, Definition <REF_0002>.\n\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-definition-regular-local}", "MATH_0001": "$(R, \\mathfrak m)$", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathfrak m$", "MATH_0003": "$\\dim(R)$", "MATH_0004": "$R$", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it ", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "MATH_0005": "$R_{\\mathfrak p}$", "MATH_0006": "$R$", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebra-definition-regular}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:5a4df33f76a78997e46e3845e8d1ccf64cd4316cd6a7c4d5c255742b92f690b8", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2a2c456d71a90dd3c11718a47ab52bad5dfcb4f39de89a51deafb60f04ab9c0d", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f850b1059dd844eeeed77b7b25e09eafb3b0a97ceed8c41191b8e89b6f90205f"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:02IS:statement", "parent_tag": "02IR", "chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "definition", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. We say <MATH_0002> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>regular<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>, or <TEXTITOPEN_0002>nonsingular<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> if\nfor every <MATH_0003> there exists an affine open neighbourhood\n<MATH_0004> of <MATH_0005> such that the ring <MATH_0006> is\nNoetherian and regular.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it ", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "MATH_0003": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0004": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0005": "$x$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U)$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-regular}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:c0a96880cc837a7b8ec4a97fc009b6be80ebee3df61c3afcfaeb1ccb7af38dba", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:44f9692731fc2cd52b6bfe020b7c2fc41e2f0bb836d95acef03dc3902917e812", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0b2eb5d6445e3fef7cf6e8525ac32f2f97d358fa8fbe445912adb428a19a6525"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:02IT:statement", "parent_tag": "02IR", "chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. The following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002> is regular,\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0003> is locally Noetherian and all of its local rings are regular,\nand\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0004> is locally Noetherian and for any closed point <MATH_0005>\nthe local ring <MATH_0006> is regular.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-characterize-regular}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:32af9ad6f10134b1c90e71b8f692a077f3a37d25e5646d8107828974ad06ab4e", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bfba6f895b6fdfc6eca76ff10ec38187bfd67d0866bebdb7d32a96ca7866c7c0", "source_math_hash": "sha256:066224f805a8414e8226d8a586a98bd42d64eab462af5b3b407ed490c33091a7"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:02IT:proof", "parent_tag": "02IR", "chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "proof", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "By the discussion in Algebra preceding Algebra, Definition\n<REF_0001> we know that the localization of\na regular local ring is regular. The lemma follows\nby combining this with Lemma <REF_0002>,\nwith the existence of closed\npoints on locally Noetherian schemes\n(Lemma <REF_0003>), and\nthe definitions.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-definition-regular}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-locally-Noetherian}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-locally-Noetherian-closed-point}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:7b8446bbf528d675b9433078500e699a822c11db923a374f1be9f60b59276833", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f147c793df45524e286cb82083c62f0d1bbda7a02fca84b9f15d0a9498075497", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:02IU:statement", "parent_tag": "02IR", "chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. The following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The scheme <MATH_0002> is regular.\n<STRUCT_0003> For every affine open <MATH_0003> the ring <MATH_0004>\nis Noetherian and regular.\n<STRUCT_0004> There exists an affine open covering <MATH_0005> such that\neach <MATH_0006> is Noetherian and regular.\n<STRUCT_0005> There exists an open covering <MATH_0007>\nsuch that each open subscheme <MATH_0008> is regular.\n<STRUCT_0006>\nMoreover, if <MATH_0009> is regular then every open subscheme is regular.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "MATH_0003": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U)$", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "MATH_0005": "$X = \\bigcup U_i$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U_i)$", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "MATH_0007": "$X = \\bigcup X_j$", "MATH_0008": "$X_j$", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}", "MATH_0009": "$X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-locally-regular}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:bc93aa26f3f63a06b7e80f613f481ed6d12f9f35f0f0f4b6e02b34a10eaf3367", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ac33417bb0163544976fd16387ebac9764a31f4f7b0449ad4578e66687d9720f", "source_math_hash": "sha256:555b2b125c46a99a2b385a173afe2abdca090cb0d8ed322725f9e75886cb4b24"}
